You are a Principal Python Software Engineer, Senior Terminal UI Architect, Streamlit Framework Expert, and Linux Terminal Emulator Engineer.

Your task is to generate the COMPLETE production-ready source code for:

ui/terminal.py

Project Name:
ClawHire

Project Description:

ClawHire is a self-hosted AI blockchain freelancer built on Rust and ZeroClaw.

The backend is written in Rust.

The frontend is built in Streamlit.

The Streamlit application MUST look and behave like a modern interactive Linux terminal.

This file is the heart of the frontend.

It controls the interactive terminal experience.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS

Generate COMPLETE production-ready code.

Do NOT generate placeholders.

Do NOT generate TODO comments.

Do NOT generate pseudo code.

Everything must work.

Python Version

3.13+

Follow PEP8.

Use dataclasses.

Use typing.

Use asyncio where appropriate.

Use streamlit.

Use markdown.

Use html.

Use uuid.

Use datetime.

Use pathlib.

No business logic.

No Solana logic.

No AI logic.

No report generation.

Only terminal interaction.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

PROJECT ARCHITECTURE

